00.00000, 000.00000␀Receiver␀␀␀␀Found automatically: when the GPS does not answer at this speed, the device tries the others and keeps the one that works. This is where it starts.␀Serial speed␀␀␀␀The GPS rests between position checks and wakes on its own. It stays awake while the map, this page or Discover is open. The battery saver turns this on too.␀␀␀Save battery␀␀␀␀Check position every␀␀␀␀Privacy␀100 m␀␀␀250 m␀␀␀1 km␀␀␀␀Exact␀␀␀Others see your advertised position shifted by up to this much; your own map keeps the real fix.␀␀␀␀Location privacy␀␀␀␀Send advert now␀Chat history␀␀␀␀250␀500␀1000␀␀␀␀2000␀␀␀␀No limit␀␀␀␀Older messages in a chat are dropped past this. A very large or unlimited history makes the chat list slower.␀␀␀Keep per chat␀␀␀After this many failed background saves the chat is saved straight away, which can stutter the screen for a moment. Off keeps retrying in the background.␀␀␀Save in the foreground after␀␀␀␀Console mode␀␀␀␀Text console␀␀␀␀Experimental. Boots into a text console with no graphical interface: type commands, read replies. Type 'ui' there to come back; if it ever fails to start, the device returns here on its own. Turning it on or off restarts.␀␀␀MediaMesh: %s␀␀␀MAIN␀␀␀␀RADIO2␀␀Live␀␀␀␀Heard main / radio2␀Sent main / radio2␀␀Share of packets heard on radio2␀␀␀␀Switch time␀Preamble main / radio2␀␀Profile switches␀␀␀␀radio2 profile␀␀On listens and sends on radio2. Applies with the button below.␀␀Bandwidth (kHz)␀Preamble␀␀␀␀Leave the preamble empty and the repeater picks it. Everyone on radio2 must use the same settings.␀␀Apply to repeater␀␀␀î“²␀Bridging␀␀␀␀Both ways␀␀␀Auto␀␀␀␀Separate␀␀␀␀Replies to admins␀␀␀Both␀␀␀␀Main␀␀␀␀Where logins, CLI answers and ACKs go out. Both is the default.␀For Both or radio2 while radio2 is set to Listen.␀␀␀Also on a listen-only radio2␀␀␀␀radio2 can't send right now, so replies only go out on the main radio.␀␀Temporary radio2␀␀␀␀Runs the profile above without saving it, for example to meet another group. The saved radio2 comes back after, or on a reboot.␀15 min␀␀1 h␀2 h␀6 h␀Running now␀Asking the repeater...␀␀A LoRa Update is running for␀␀␀␀LoRa Update␀Firmware file␀␀␀v%u.%u.%u.%u␀␀␀␀v%u.%u.%u␀␀␀%s  %s  %s␀␀îƒŒ␀Build .mota files with Mike Carper's motatool, or download them in MeshCore Open TAK. Use a file made for this repeater's board.␀␀␀␀Temporary radio␀The repeater and this radio meet here for the transfer, away from the normal mesh. Pick a quiet frequency you may use. The repeater must be in direct range.␀␀␀␀Minutes␀Step␀␀␀␀Blocks␀␀Packets sent␀␀␀␀Start update␀␀␀␀Install and reboot␀␀Log␀This radio can't run a temporary radio (its SX1262 signals packets through an I/O expander), so it can't serve updates.␀This radio can't run a temporary radio (needs an SX1262), so it can't serve updates.␀␀␀␀Custom (manual)␀Picking one applies it straight away.␀␀␀Community preset␀␀␀␀TX dBm␀␀AF␀␀SF is the spreading factor, CR the coding rate, AF the airtime factor. A field applies when you leave it.␀␀␀Max duty cycle␀␀Time on air␀radio2 (MediaMesh)␀␀This radio can't run a second frequency. Its SX1262 signals a packet through an I/O expander, not straight to the processor, so it can't hop between two frequencies quickly enough. The Terminal still takes tempradio.␀␀␀␀This radio can't run a second frequency. It needs an SX1262, LR1110, LR1121 or LR2021 radio. The Terminal still takes tempradio.␀␀␀␀A second frequency the radio switches to and from, listening and sending there.␀Photos & voice␀␀Everything␀␀Photos & voice: Open TAK photos and voice clips, text stays on the main mesh. Everything: every message goes out on both. Per contact or channel: their Radio setting.␀␀Sent on radio2␀␀Share with them␀MediaMesh only: photo and voice requests and answers stay on radio2, so nodes without it can't swap them with you. Share: requests go out on both, and a photo or clip asked for on the main mesh is answered there.␀␀␀␀Main-mesh nodes␀Client repeat is on, so radio2 is Off: everything, photos and voice too, goes out on the main radio. radio2 goes back to how it was when Client repeat is turned off.␀␀␀250 kHz sends photos and voice about twice as fast; 125 kHz reaches about 40% farther. Both SF7, CR 4/5. Everyone on radio2 must use the same.␀␀Preset␀␀Find MediaMesh␀␀ï„¤␀Listening...␀␀␀␀Found␀␀␀Find MediaMesh listens on each preset for about 10 s while nearby repeaters are asked to answer. MediaMesh repeaters answer on radio2 too, so the preset they're heard on is the one in use here.␀␀␀Everyone sharing radio2 must use the same settings. The radio switches between both frequencies, so heavy radio2 traffic costs some main-mesh reception.␀␀␀␀Listen main / radio2␀␀␀␀radio2 preamble␀Packets main / radio2␀␀␀Warnings␀␀␀␀Use other radio2 settings for a while, for example to meet another group. They end on their own or on a restart; the settings above come back.␀␀2 hours␀Use these for␀␀␀Battery and sensor readings, for nodes that ask. Your location has its own setting below.␀␀␀Answer telemetry requests␀␀␀Most mesh spam is a single character, because it is the cheapest message to send. Dropped silently: no chat entry, no notification, no sound.␀␀␀Ignore 1-character messages␀Location sharing␀␀␀␀Chosen contacts only␀␀␀␀Anyone who asks␀Sent only when that contact asks, encrypted to them. Nothing is broadcast. Needs "Answer telemetry requests" on. Pick contacts in a contact's menu.␀Share my location when asked␀␀␀␀Off sends them the shifted position your adverts use (GPS > Location privacy).␀␀Exact position to those contacts␀␀␀␀Routing␀1 byte␀␀2 bytes␀3 bytes␀More bytes tell repeaters apart in a big mesh. Repeaters older than MeshCore 1.14 drop 2 and 3 byte packets.␀␀␀␀Multi-byte routing (path hash)␀␀#region␀Region scope (#tag, blank = none)␀␀␀Channel-specific regions can be set in each channel's settings.␀Known regions␀␀␀Turn on only if your repeater re-floods just one region. Otherwise it can block logins and direct messages across regions.␀␀Scope direct msgs to region␀